ips (roughly 60-75% pot). Here's why:\n\n1. I likely have the best hand with top pair, top kicker\n2. The board is draw-heavy (flush and straight possibilities)\n3. Opponent's check shows weakness - they likely don't have a strong made hand\n4. I need to charge drawing hands and protect my equity\n5. A bet here is standard and represents my pre-flop aggression\n6. Checking gives a free card which is dangerous on this coordinated board\n\nBetting 800 accomplishes multiple goals: extracts value from worse hands, protects against draws, and maintains initiative. It's large enough to make draws pay incorrectly but not so large that I'm overcommitting to a one-pair hand.\n\nAnswer: 800"}
